1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. c3 dxc3 5. Nxc3 e6 6. Be3 Nc6 7. Be2 b5 {
To prevent 8 Na4-b6} 8. O-O d6 9. Rc1 Bd7 ({If} 9... Bb7 {he may sacrifice on
b5 (later) and I wouldn't want my knight pinned.}) 10. Nd4 Rc8 ({If, say,} 
10... Nf6 11. Nxc6 Bxc6 12. Na4 {may be good for White.}) 11. a3 Nf6 12. f4 Be7
13. g4 h6 14. g5 ({Rather premature. Very good was} 14. Bd3 {then his queen
has access to h5 in the variations below.}) 14... hxg5 15. fxg5 Nh7 16. Rxf7 $2
({Aggressive but unsound. Black's position is stronger than it looks. Correct
was} 16. g6 fxg6 17. Bh5 $1) 16... Kxf7 17. g6+ {[60'] White has nothing
better than this.} ({If} 17. Bh5+ Kg8) 17... Kg8 {[35']} 18. gxh7+ {[73']
Again White has nothing better.} Rxh7 {[36']} 19. Bg4 {[86']} Bg5 {[44']
Absolutely crushing.} 20. Bxg5 {[94']} Qxg5 {[44']} 21. Nxc6 {[106']} Rxc6 {
[47']} 22. Kh1 g6 {[54']} 23. Qg1 {Threat 24.Bxe6+} Qf4 24. Bxe6+ {[120']} (24.
Rf1 Rxh2+ $1) 24... Bxe6 25. Qxg6+ {[121']} Kh8 {[61']} 26. Qg1 {[133']} Qf3+ {
Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.}
({and not the clever} 26... Rxh2+ {because the Queen takes with check.} 27.
Qxh2+) 0-1

