1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 c6 4. Bg2 d5 5. cxd5 cxd5 6. Nf3 Bd7 {Rather an odd
idea as the Bishop doesn't serve a purpopse here.} 7. O-O Bg7 8. Nc3 Bc6 9. Ne5
O-O 10. b4 {Attempting to take advantage of the positioning of the Bishop.} b6
({If} 10... Qb6 11. Rb1) 11. Qb3 Bb7 12. e3 Nbd7 13. Nd3 {I hoped to play 14.
b5, 16Nb4, 17Nc6 I can't win the d-Pawn.} ({I didn't like} 13. f4) 13... e6 14.
a4 Ne4 15. Nxe4 {As the knight was immobilising my c1-bishop.} dxe4 16. Nf4 g5
({I expected} 16... e5) 17. Ne2 ({Not} 17. Nxe6 fxe6 18. Qxe6+ Kh8 19. Bxe4 Re8
) 17... Bd5 18. Qb1 f5 19. f3 {I must take some positive action on the KS.} Nf6
20. Nc3 exf3 {[75']} 21. Nxd5 {[45'] Doubtful. I didn't realise how strong a
position Black gets.} fxg2 22. Nxf6+ Rxf6 23. Kxg2 Qd5+ 24. Kg1 f4 25. exf4 ({
The only move everything else loses, e.g.} 25. Qd3 fxg3 26. hxg3 Rh6) (25. Qa2
fxg3 26. hxg3 Rxf1+ 27. Kxf1 Qh1+) (25. gxf4 gxf4 {etc.}) 25... gxf4 ({If} 
25... Qxd4+ 26. Rf2 {threatens 27.Bb2}) 26. Bxf4 Qxd4+ 27. Kg2 ({Not} 27. Rf2
Rxf4 $1) 27... e5 (27... Qd5+ $142) 28. Qb3+ Kh8 29. Be3 Qe4+ 30. Kg1 Rc6 {
Threat 31......Rc2} 31. Rac1 Rac8 32. Rxc6 Rxc6 33. Rd1 Rc8 ({Not} 33... h6 34.
Rd8+) 34. Rd7 Qf3 {Threat 35...Rc1+} 35. Qd3 $1 Rf8 {[145']} 36. Bh6 {[116']
Giving Black, in time-trouble, a chance to go wrong.} Qxd3 {Correct.} 37. Bxg7+
Kg8 38. Rxd3 Kxg7 39. Rd7+ {Probably not best but I was trying to rush Black
into a mistake.} Rf7 40. Rd2 Rc7 41. a5 {I was running short of time myself
here and some of these moves are doubtful.} bxa5 42. bxa5 Kf6 43. Kf2 Ke6 44.
Ra2 {I didn't mean to play this but suddenly realised how short of time I was
and picked up the rook by mistake.} Rc3 45. a6 {I offered a draw here.} Kf5 {
[149']} 46. Ke2 {[149'] The sealed move.} (46. Ke2 {During the adjournment I
came to the conclusion that the position was drawn, e.g.} e4 (46... Kg4 47.
Ra4+ Kh3 $2 48. Rh4+ {etc.}) (46... h5 47. Kf2 Z0 48. Ke2 {etc}) 47. Rb2 Ra3
48. Rb7 Rxa6 49. Rxh7) 46... h6 {It looks like the game was concluded the next
morning, 4/4/64. As Dick makes reference to keeping an opponent waiting for
the a.m. tournament he entered in the same week! (Sean Parker)} 47. Rd2 $1 Rc6
({If} 47... Ra3 48. Rd6 $18 h5 49. Rh6 Ra2+ 50. Ke3 Rxh2 51. Rh7 {etc}) 48. Ra2
Ke4 49. Ra4+ Kd5 50. Ra5+ Kd6 51. Ra2 Rb6 52. Kd3 Rb1 53. Ke3 Rb4 54. Kd3 {
[164']} Kc5 55. Ra5+ Kd6 56. Ra2 Rd4+ 57. Ke3 Ke6 58. Rc2 Rd6 59. Ra2 Kf5 60.
Rf2+ Ke6 61. Ra2 Rb6 62. Kd3 $2 {Giving away the half point after all my hard
work. I thought that Black was getting nowhere and I was playing very quickly
as I was supposed to have started my game in the morning speed event 2hrs
previously and I had kept my opponent waiting all that time hence I was
rushing and gave the game away.} (62. Ke2 $1 {would have drawn. c.f. the
sealed move position.}) 62... Kf5 63. Rf2+ Kg4 64. Ra2 Kf3 65. Kd2 e4 66. Ra3+
Kf2 67. h4 Rd6+ 68. Kc1 e3 69. Ra5 e2 70. Rf5+ {A pity that I had to rush the
ending. Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19
December 2022.} 0-1

