O-O O-O 9. Be3 Be6 10. Qc1 ({10 Qc1 is much better than} 10. a3 a5 {as played
against P.M.Collins.}) 10... h6 {Prevents 11 Ng5 followed by 12 Nxe6.} 11. Ne4
f5 12. Nc5 Bxc5 13. Bxc5 Rf7 14. b4 Nd7 (14... a6 {may be an improvement.}) 15.
b5 Ne7 16. Bxe7 Rxe7 17. Qc3 {[64']} Bd5 {[29']} 18. e4 fxe4 19. dxe4 Bf7 ({
White is well on top now. Not} 19... Bxe4 $4 20. Qc4+) 20. Rfd1 Qc8 21. Rd2 c6
22. Rad1 {[93']} Qc7 {[48']} 23. bxc6 bxc6 24. Rd6 c5 25. a3 Rb8 26. Bh3 Rb3
27. Qd2 ({Not} 27. Rxd7 $2 Rxc3 $1) 27... Rxf3 28. Bxd7 Rxa3 $2 29. Rc6 $1 Qb7
30. Qd6 ({I expected} 30. Rc8+ Kh7 31. Qd6 Z0 32. Bf5+ $140) 30... Rxd7 31.
Qxd7 Qxd7 32. Rxd7 Bh5 33. Kg2 $2 ({I was expecting} 33. Rxc5) 33... Bf3+ 34.
Kh3 Bxe4 35. Rd8+ Kh7 36. Rxc5 Bf5+ 37. Kg2 Be4+ 38. Kf1 Bd3+ 39. Ke1 e4 40.
Rd7 Ra1+ 41. Kd2 Ra2+ 42. Ke3 Re2+ 43. Kd4 Rxf2 44. Rcc7 Rxh2 $4 {A stupid
error due to tiredness. It was now 6pm and I had been playing since 9.30 with
only a 25 minute break. The result of entering too many tournaments at once.}
45. Rxg7+ Kh8 46. Rgd7 Bc4 47. Kxc4 {Source: Dick Collins scorebook,
contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} ({Not} 47. Rxc4 $2 Rd2+) 1-0

