1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Ne2 ({If} 5. Bd3 {he can safely take
the d-Pawm. I hoped to transpose into the usual 3......Nf6 variation.}) 5...
Nf6 6. e5 Nd7 7. Nf3 cxd4 8. cxd4 Bb4+ 9. Nc3 ({If} 9. Bd2 Bxd2+ 10. Qxd2 Qa5 {
is OK for Black . I didn't want to simplify by exchanges.}) 9... a6 10. Bd3 Be7
{leaving his king uncommitted.} 11. O-O b5 12. a3 Nb6 13. Qc2 Bb7 $1 {Correct.
His King is able to go to d7. c.f. variation blow.} ({If} 13... Bd7 $2 14. Bxh7
$1 g6 15. Bxg6 fxg6 16. Qxg6+ Kf8 17. Bh6+) 14. Ne2 {If I can play the Knight
to f4 I can play the above variation as ......Kd7 can be answered by Qxe6+} Rc8
15. Qb1 h6 {Preventing the Bxh6 variation.} ({I expected.} 15... b4) 16. Nf4
Kd7 {With the mistaken idea of pushing on the KS} 17. Be3 h5 (17... g5 18. Nh5)
18. Nd2 g5 19. Ne2 f5 20. exf6 Bxf6 21. f4 {Showing up Black's faulty strategy.
} Nc4 22. fxg5 Bxg5 23. Rf7+ Be7 24. Nxc4 bxc4 25. Bg6 ({Also good is} 25. Bc2
Z0 26. Ba4) 25... Qg8 26. Nf4 Rf8 27. Rxf8 Qxf8 28. Bxh5 Bg5 29. Qg6 {The only
move. I thought it won easily, not having seen his 30th move.} Bxf4 30. Bxf4
Rxh5 $1 ({Best. If} 30... Rg8 31. Qh7+ Rg7 32. Qh6 Nxd4 33. Be5) 31. Qxh5 Qxf4
32. Qh7+ Ne7 33. Qg7 Bc6 {He offered a draw here.} 34. Re1 $1 ({Not too good is
} 34. Rf1 Qe3+ 35. Kh1 Bb5) 34... Ba4 35. g3 {This move, opening White
diagonals, may lose. I thought I could get the KS pawns moving.} Qf5 ({If} 
35... Qd2 36. Qe5) 36. h4 ({Not} 36. Rf1 Qc2 37. Rf7 Qc1+ 38. Kg2 $2 Qxb2+ 39.
Kh3 Qxa3) 36... Bc2 37. Re2 {In a quandary here. This strengthens the QS.} Be4
38. Rf2 {I offered a draw here.} Qh5 39. Qf8 ({I'm lost. If} 39. Rf7 Qd1+ 40.
Kf2 (40. Kh2 $4 Qh1#) 40... Qc2+ 41. Kf1 Qc1+ 42. Kf2 Qxb2+ 43. Ke1 Qxa3) 39...
Qd1+ 40. Rf1 Qxd4+ 41. Kh2 Bf5 42. Qb8 Qd2+ 43. Kg1 Qe3+ 44. Rf2 Qxg3+ $4 {
Black immediately realised his hasty blunder and resigned. Source: Dick
Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 1-0

