1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 {[7']} e5 {[1']} 6. Nf5 {[28']
} d5 7. Ng3 {[28']} d4 {[4']} 8. Nb1 {[38']} Nc6 {[9']} 9. Bd3 {[40']} Bc5 10.
Nd2 {[46']} b5 {[15']} 11. Nb3 Ba7 12. Bd2 Qb6 {Prevents 13.c3} 13. Nc1 Be6 {
[22']} 14. O-O {[62']} Nd7 15. b4 {Very committal.} Qc7 {[30']} 16. Nb3 {[72']}
Qd6 {[36']} 17. a3 {[82']} Bxb3 {May be wrong for though I get a passed Pawn
he gets good play on the QS.} 18. cxb3 O-O {[45'] Dangerous.} ({If} 18... g6
19. Bh6) 19. Nf5 {[85']} Qe6 {[47']} 20. a4 {[90'] Very strong. He threatens
to win my b-Pawn.} bxa4 {[58']} 21. Bc4 $1 ({I missed this. It's very strong.
Intending to answer} 21. bxa4 {with} a5 22. bxa5 Nc5) 21... Qf6 22. Bd5 $1 Rac8
23. Qg4 {[98'] Again very strong.} (23. Qg4 {the threat is......} Z0 24. Bg5
Qg6 25. Bxc6 Z0 26. Ne7+) 23... Kh8 $1 {[78'] The only move.} 24. bxa4 {[102']}
({If now} 24. Bg5 Qg6 25. Bxc6 Rxc6 26. Ne7 Qe6 $1) 24... Nb6 {[85']} 25. Bb3 (
25. Bb3 {The threat is.....} Z0 26. b5 axb5 27. axb5) 25... Rc7 {[97']} 26. b5
{[113']} Nb8 {[99'] Playing too quickly thinking that I had survived the worst.
} 27. a5 axb5 28. axb6 Bxb6 29. Bd5 Bc5 30. Rab1 g6 {The b-pawn can't be
defended. Now we get some fireworks.} 31. Bg5 Qb6 32. Rxb5 $3 gxf5 33. Qxf5 Qg6
34. Bf6+ $2 (34. Qxe5+ $1 {wins straight off.}) 34... Kg8 35. Qxe5 Rcc8 {
Threat 36......Nd7} 36. Qf4 Nd7 37. e5 Nxf6 {This may or may not have been
best.} 38. exf6 Rfd8 {I was again playing too quickly.} (38... Rfe8 $142) 39.
Be4 Qh5 ({If} 39... Bd6 40. Qh4 $1) 40. Qg3+ Kf8 41. Qg7+ Ke8 42. Rb7 Rd7 (
42... Bf8 43. Qg8 $1 {Threatens mate.}) 43. Qg8+ Bf8 44. Re1 Qe5 ({If} 44...
Qe2 45. Rbb1) 45. f4 ({Not} 45. Rxd7 Kxd7 46. Bc6+ $4 Rxc6) 45... Qa5 46. Re2
Rc1+ {I can hang on no longer.} 47. Kf2 Rxb7 48. Bxb7+ Kd7 49. Qxf7+ Kd6 50.
Qxf8+ Kc7 51. Qc8+ {Very interesting. White played well after the opening and
I played well at times but unfortunately relaxed my concentration after move
25. Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December
2022.} 1-0

