1. c4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Nf3 e6 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 Nbd7 7. Bd3 dxc4 8.
Bxc4 O-O (8... Nd5 {was also good}) 9. e4 {In need of a win I played
aggressively} h6 (9... c5 {was possibly better.}) 10. Bf4 Nb6 ({Not a good
move. If} 10... c5 11. d5 exd5 12. exd5 Z0 13. d6) 11. Bd3 Nh5 12. Be3 f5 $2 {
very loosening} 13. Ne5 Qe8 (13... Nf6 $142 {as I can win a Pawn fairly safely.
}) 14. exf5 exf5 15. Qb3+ Kh8 16. g4 $1 {Winning a pawn. Black gets unduly
despondent about this and decides on a desperate but futile sacrifice.} Bd6 $2
({After} 16... Nf6 17. gxf5 {both replies are good} (17. g5)) 17. gxh5 Bxe5 18.
dxe5 Qxe5 {For his piece Black hopes to get an attack and to pick up some of
my loose Pawns. However, I get the attack and some of his Pawns.} 19. O-O-O Be6
20. Qb4 Nd5 21. Qd4 Qxd4 ({Not} 21... Qc7 $2 22. Bxh6) (21... Qd6 $2 22. Bxh6)
22. Bxd4 Nxc3 23. Bxc3 Bxa2 {I soon get the Pawn back on the KS} 24. Rhg1 Rf7
25. Rg6 {Threat 26 Rxh6+.} Kg8 26. Rdg1 Rd8 27. Rxg7+ Rxg7 28. Rxg7+ Kf8 29.
Bxf5 Bb3 {Threatening mate, no less!} 30. Bc2 Bxc2 31. Kxc2 Rd5 32. Rg6 Rxh5
33. Bg7+ Kf7 34. Rxh6 Rc5+ 35. Bc3 Rf5 36. Bd4 c5 37. Be3 b5 38. Rh7+ Ke6 39.
Rxa7 Kd5 40. Rc7 Kc4 41. b3+ {Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by
Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 1-0

