1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. O-O e5 5. d3 g6 6. Nbd2 Bg7 7. e4 Nge7 8. c3
h6 ({If} 8... O-O 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nc4 {and I can't play} Be6 {so as to be
able to answer} 11. Re1 {with} Qc7) 9. Qa4 a6 $2 {Underestimating White's last.
I was playing too casually in this game.} ({Correct was} 9... O-O) 10. exd5 b5
({Now if} 10... Nxd5 11. Qc4 {wins at least the c-pawn. This may have been
Black's best.}) 11. Qa3 Qxd5 {Protects everything but only for one move.} 12.
c4 ({Not} 12. Nxe5 $2 Qxe5) 12... b4 ({Loses but the best chance. If} 12...
bxc4 13. Nxc4 Bb7 {say} 14. Nfxe5) 13. cxd5 bxa3 14. dxc6 e4 15. Nxe4 axb2 16.
Bxb2 Bxb2 17. Rab1 Ba3 18. Nd6+ {White has an easy win being a Pawn up, better
developed and better positioned.} Kf8 19. Nc4 Bb4 20. a3 Bc3 21. Rfc1 Bd4 (
21... Bf6 {may be a bit better but I had given up.}) 22. Nxd4 cxd4 23. Nb6 Ra7
({If} 23... Rb8 24. c7) 24. Nxc8 Nxc8 25. Rb4 Ke7 26. Rxd4 Nd6 {Putting a
quick end to it.} 27. Re1+ {I had rather given up trying and played the whole
game too lethargically. Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean
Parker, 19 December 2022.} 1-0

