1. d4 d5 2. e3 Nf6 3. Bd3 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. f4 Bg4 6. Nf3 e6 7. Nbd2 {I hadn't
played this opening before and didn't know it too well.} (7. O-O $142 {as I
can capture on d4 with the e-Pawn}) 7... Bd6 8. O-O cxd4 9. cxd4 O-O 10. a3 Bf5
$2 {There is no reason to let his Pawns be weakened.} 11. Bxf5 exf5 12. Ne5 Rc8
13. b4 Ne4 14. Nb3 b6 15. b5 Ne7 16. Bb2 f6 17. Nf3 Nc3 18. Qd3 Na4 19. Rf2 Qd7
20. Nc1 $1 Rc7 21. Qb3 Nxb2 22. Rxb2 Rfc8 23. Ne2 Qe6 24. Nd2 {Now I have all
the play the c-file being useless to Black.} Ng6 25. g3 h5 26. Raa2 h4 27. a4
hxg3 28. hxg3 Rc3 $6 {This is unsound. Black overestimates his position.} 29.
Nxc3 Qxe3+ 30. Kg2 Rxc3 31. Qxd5+ Kh7 32. Qf3 Bxf4 $1 33. Qxe3 Bxe3 34. Nf3 f4
35. g4 Ne7 36. Rc2 Rd3 37. Rc7 Nd5 38. Rxa7 Bxd4 39. Nxd4 Rxd4 40. Ra3 Ne3+ 41.
Kf3 Nc2 42. Rc3 Ne1+ 43. Kf2 Nd3+ 44. Ke2 Ne5 45. Rcc7 $2 {As all through the
tournament I had been playing too quickly and also rather unambitiously
towards the end.} f3+ 46. Kf1 Rd1+ 47. Kf2 Rd2+ 48. Kf1 $4 {Playing on
completely oblivious to Black's intentions.} (48. Kg3 $142) 48... Nd3 49. Rxg7+
Kh6 50. g5+ Kh5 {Still playing at great speed with too little effort. Source:
Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} ({Not} 
50... fxg5 51. Rh7+ Kg6 52. Rhg7+ Kf5 53. Raf7+ Kg4 54. Rxg5+ {With drawing
chances.}) 0-1

