1. d4 d5 2. e3 Nf6 3. Bd3 c5 4. c3 Nbd7 5. f4 g6 6. Nf3 Bg7 7. O-O O-O 8. h3 e6
{[21']} 9. Nbd2 {[9']} Qe7 10. g4 c4 {Doubtful eases the tension in the centre.
} 11. Bc2 b5 12. Qe2 {I wanted to play something like 12.f5 but my e-Pawn
needed defending.} Bb7 13. Rf2 Ne4 $2 {Loses a pawn.} 14. Nxe4 dxe4 15. Nd2 f5
16. a4 a6 17. b3 {Wins a Pawn in view of the threat of 18 Ba3.} Rfc8 $8 18. Bb2
({If now} 18. bxc4 bxc4 19. Nxc4 Bd5) 18... Bd5 {He can't really save the Pawn.
Now I win a pawn.} 19. axb5 $1 axb5 20. bxc4 $2 ({Terrible. I went to play 20
Rxa1 and for some unknown reason picked up the b-pawn. Typical of this
tournament where everything is going wrong. I could win a pawn by} 20. Rxa8
Rxa8 21. bxc4 {etc. I saw this and the variation....} Ra2 22. cxd5 Rxb2 23. Bb3
{etc.}) 20... Rxa1+ 21. Bxa1 bxc4 22. g5 Qa3 23. Rf1 Nb6 24. Rb1 Na4 25. Bxa4
Qxa4 26. Qf1 Ra8 27. Qc1 Bf8 28. h4 Qa2 29. Bb2 {Threat 30.Ra1} Rb8 30. Kf1 Bd6
$1 {Threat 31...Bxf4!} 31. Ke2 Kf7 $22 32. Ke1 ({If} 32. Kf2 Ba3 $1 $19) 32...
Ke8 $2 {here I offered a draw which he accepted. For the second time in this
tournament I pick up a piece by mistake after working out the correct move.
Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.}
({Why not?} 32... Bxf4 {I intended} 33. exf4 e3 34. Nxc4 {but it's doubtful})
1/2-1/2

