1. e4 g6 2. Nf3 Bg7 3. c3 d6 4. d4 Nf6 5. Be2 O-O $2 6. O-O $2 Nbd7 $2 {
We both started off at lightning speed and overlooked White's e-Pawn was
en-prise.} 7. Qd3 a6 8. a4 e5 9. dxe5 Nc5 10. Qd1 Nfxe4 11. exd6 Nxd6 12. Be3
Nce4 13. Nbd2 Qe7 {I needed to win this game to ntry for 1st prize so I was
willing to take risks to try to win. Unfortunately White made no attempt to
win, trying only for a draw.} 14. Nxe4 Nxe4 15. Bd4 Rd8 16. Qc2 Bh6 {Trying
not to simplify.} 17. Bd3 c5 $6 {Desperately trying to create chances.} 18.
Bxe4 cxd4 19. Nxd4 Bg4 20. h3 Be6 21. Rad1 Bd5 22. Bxd5 Rxd5 23. Rfe1 Qc7 24.
Qe4 Rd7 25. Nf3 Rad8 26. Rxd7 Rxd7 27. Nd4 Bf4 28. Qe2 {He offered a draw here.
(Even though a Pawn up!)} Bd6 29. Qd2 Be5 30. Qe3 Re7 31. Kh1 Qb6 $6 {A last
try.} 32. Nf3 Qxb2 33. Nxe5 f6 {Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by
Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 1/2-1/2

